Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was the use of the `devm_request_threaded_irq` function to register CEC interrupt handlers, which automatically managed the freeing of the interrupt request but did so after the device resources were unbound or if the binding failed. This created a scenario where the interrupt handler could be invoked after the device had been unbound but before the resources it depended on were cleaned up, potentially leading to unsafe access to freed memory. The solution involved switching to the non-devm variant of the IRQ request function to allow for better control over the timing of the IRQ handler's unregistration, ensuring safety in resource management.
